          "gloss": "tamarisk tree",
          "definition": "A tree that can be planted and can serve as a recognisable landmark. Arabic and South Arabian tree names support the identification as a tamarisk.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "ref": "Gen.21.33",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "Abraham plants the tree at Beersheba and calls there on Yahweh’s name."
            },
            {
              "ref": "1Sa.22.6",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "Saul sits beneath the tree on the height at Gibeah, with his servants standing around him."
            },
            {
              "ref": "1Sa.31.13",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "The people of Jabesh bury the bones of Saul and his sons beneath the tree and fast seven days."
            }
